{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-853252e8ee64d886","type":"tool_result","content":"557\t// deferIfAtConcurrencyCap reports whether the agent is already running its\n558\t// configured maximum number of Jobs, and if so registers the task for a\n559\t// deferred respawn instead of spawning now.\n560\t//\n561\t// Deferring rather than skipping is the whole point. Task publication is\n562\t// edge-triggered on vault file changes; being over the cap produces no such\n563\t// change, so a skipped spawn would never be re-driven and the task would sit\n564\t// at in_progress forever, indistinguishable from work in flight.\n565\tfunc (h *taskEventHandler) deferIfAtConcurrencyCap(\n566\t\tctx context.Context,\n567\t\ttask lib.Task,\n568\t\tconfig *pkg.AgentConfiguration,\n569\t) (bool, error) {\n570\t\tif config == nil || config.MaxConcurrentJobs <= 0 {\n571\t\t\treturn false, nil\n572\t\t}\n573\t\trunning, err := h.jobSpawner.CountActiveJobs(ctx, config.Assignee)\n574\t\tif err != nil {\n575\t\t\tmetrics.TaskEventsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"error\").Inc()\n576\t\t\treturn false, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"count active jobs for assignee %s\", config.Assignee)\n577\t\t}\n578\t\tif running < config.MaxConcurrentJobs {\n579\t\t\t// Log the ADMIT decision, not just the deferral. Without this, an\n580\t\t\t// over-cap spawn leaves no trace and overshoot can only be found by\n581\t\t\t// counting Jobs in the cluster by hand — which is how the 2026-08-15\n582\t\t\t// race went unnoticed until 17 Jobs existed against a cap of 1.\n583\t\t\t// Same V(1) rationale as the deferral log below.\n584\t\t\tglog.V(1).Infof(\n585\t\t\t\t\"event=concurrency_admit task=%s assignee=%s running=%d cap=%d\",\n586\t\t\t\ttask.TaskIdentifier, config.Assignee, running, config.MaxConcurrentJobs,\n587\t\t\t)\n588\t\t\treturn false, nil\n589\t\t}\n590\t\t// V(1), not V(0): a capped deferral is an expected steady state and repeats\n591\t\t// once per retry interval per waiting task, so V(0) would be a constant\n592\t\t// stream during any backlog. V(1) is inside the deployed verbosity, so it\n593\t\t// stays visible to an operator looking — unlike the V(3) skip that hid the\n594\t\t// wedge fixed in #12.\n595\t\tglog.V(1).Infof(\n596\t\t\t\"event=concurrency_cap task=%s assignee=%s running=%d cap=%d retry_after=%s\",\n597\t\t\ttask.TaskIdentifier, config.Assignee, running, config.MaxConcurrentJobs,\n598\t\t\tconcurrencyCapRetryDelay,\n599\t\t)\n600\t\tmetrics.TaskEventsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"deferred_concurrency_cap\").Inc()\n601\t\th.deferredMu.Lock()\n602\t\th.deferredRespawns[task.TaskIdentifier] = deferredEntry{\n603\t\t\ttask:       task,\n604\t\t\tconfig:     *config,\n605\t\t\tretryAfter: h.currentDateTime.Now().Time().Add(concurrencyCapRetryDelay),\n606\t\t}\n607\t\th.deferredMu.Unlock()\n608\t\treturn true, nil\n609\t}\n610\t\n611\t// evalDeferredRespawns checks all pending deferred-respawn entries and spawns a job\n612\t// for each entry whose retryAfter has been reached. Entries are removed once processed.\n613\t// The respawn_after_grace_window metric and log line fire ONLY when the call actually\n614\t// results in a spawn (spec 037 AC #6: \"recorded each time the follow-up evaluation\n615\t// results in a spawn\"); evaluations that no-op (active job already, trigger cap hit,\n616\t// terminal phase) do not increment the metric.\n617\tfunc (h *taskEventHandler) evalDeferredRespawns(ctx context.Context) error {\n618\t\tnow := h.currentDateTime.Now().Time()\n619\t\n620\t\th.deferredMu.Lock()\n621\t\tvar ready []deferredEntry\n622\t\tfor taskID, entry := range h.deferredRespawns {\n623\t\t\tif !now.Before(entry.retryAfter) {\n624\t\t\t\tready = append(ready, entry)\n625\t\t\t\tdelete(h.deferredRespawns, taskID)\n626\t\t\t}\n627\t\t}\n628\t\th.deferredMu.Unlock()\n629\t\n630\t\tfor _, entry := range ready {\n631\t\t\tentry := entry // capture for closure\n632\t\t\tspawned, err := h.spawnIfNeeded(ctx, entry.task, &entry.config)\n633\t\t\tif err != nil {\n634\t\t\t\treturn errors.Wrapf(\n635\t\t\t\t\tctx, err, \"deferred respawn for task %s\", entry.task.TaskIdentifier,\n636\t\t\t\t)\n637\t\t\t}\n638\t\t\tif !spawned {\n639\t\t\t\tcontinue\n640\t\t\t}\n641\t\t\tjobStartedAt, _ := entry.task.Frontmatter.JobStartedAt()\n642\t\t\telapsed := now.Sub(jobStartedAt)\n643\t\t\tglog.Infof(\n644\t\t\t\t\"event=respawn_after_grace_window task=%s current_job=%s elapsed=%.0fs\",\n645\t\t\t\tentry.task.TaskIdentifier, entry.task.Frontmatter.CurrentJob(), elapsed.Seconds(),\n646\t\t\t)\n647\t\t\tmetrics.TaskEventsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"respawn_after_grace_window\").Inc()\n648\t\t}\n649\t\treturn nil\n650\t}\n651\t\n652\t// removeDeferredEntry removes any pending deferred-respawn entry for the given task.\n653\t// Called from parseAndFilter when a terminal-phase event arrives so no stale spawn fires.\n654\tfunc (h *taskEventHandler) removeDeferredEntry(id lib.TaskIdentifier) {\n655\t\th.deferredMu.Lock()\n656\t\tdelete(h.deferredRespawns, id)\n657\t\th.deferredMu.Unlock()\n658\t}\n659\t\n660\t// EvalDeferredRespawns implements TaskEventHandler.\n661\tfunc (h *taskEventHandler) EvalDeferredRespawns(ctx context.Context) error {\n662\t\treturn h.evalDeferredRespawns(ctx)\n663\t}\n664\t\n665\t// seedDeferredRespawnsFromStore scans the in-memory taskStore for tasks that look\n666\t// like in-flight work (current_job set, phase non-terminal) and adds them to"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57301c7a-f90b-492d-a40b-678af5f2ac81","uuid":"cf1d028a-2223-4f7b-bfac-bc5bbdc60877","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:35:23.451Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/pkg/handler/task_event_handler.go","content":"// deferIfAtConcurrencyCap reports whether the agent is already running its\n// configured maximum number of Jobs, and if so registers the task for a\n// deferred respawn instead of spawning now.\n//\n// Deferring rather than skipping is the whole point. Task publication is